# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# This repo is edited from two hosts: a Windows workstation (CRLF by default)
# and the Linux A1 server. Without this file the same content committed from
# each host produces a whole-file diff, because every line differs by \r.
#
# That is not cosmetic. On 2026-08-08 the A1 server had six unpushed commits
# and `git diff` reported ~277 changed lines in files whose actual content was
# identical, so the real divergence was invisible without passing -w to every
# diff. Normalising means a diff shows changed *code*.
#
# NOTE: existing files are normalised lazily, as each is next staged. To
# convert the whole tree in one commit (do this only when no agent session or
# live run has uncommitted work in flight):
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only entry points must keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Gradle wrapper: the shell script must stay LF, the batch file CRLF.
gradlew     text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries git must never inspect or convert.
*.jar   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.nbt   binary
*.schem binary
